      "text": "Tautologies",
      "links": [],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Tautological self-description",
      "links": [],
      "level": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The tautology is the conceptual equivalent of the monochrome.\nIt is the proposition which is necessarily true; stating its truth thus conveys\nno information. (In Kantian terms: a tautology expresses an analytic judgment.) Prototypical tautologies are the truths of logic and mathematics.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A circular statement may be tautological\nin that its very form guarantees its truth. (\"Dit\nis Nederlands.\" \"This sentence consists of six words.\")\nSuch self-referentially true statements are sometimes presented\nas visual artworks: painted verbal descriptions which state\na self-evident property of the painting itself.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In conceptual art, this strategy is used so often that it is sometimes taken to be the defining characteristic of this artistic genre. Commenting on On Kawara's Date\nPaintings, Gudrun Inboden asserts: \"Dass die einzelne Arbeit nichts mitteilt, was über den ablesbaren Tatbestand hinausginge, und nichts außer sich selbst verkörpert (hier ihre an einen bestimmten Tag geknüpfte Entstehung), ist das spezifische Merkmal von Konzeptkunst.\" [Cf. Staatsgalerie Stuttgart: On Kawara.]",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Staatsgalerie Stuttgart: On Kawara",
          "href": "http://www.staatsgalerie.de/gemaeldeundskulpturen/n45_rundg.php?id=12",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Self-referential statements need not be\ntautological. They may be contingently true, contingently false,\nor paradoxical. The latter case arises when a statement implies\nits own falsehood; i.e., its circularity is vicious.\n(The prototype example is the liar paradox: \"I am\nlying now.\" ) Paradoxical statements constitute a\ndistinct subgenre of conceptual art; we anthologize it on a separate\npage.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "separate page",
          "href": "/concept/paradox",
          "external": false
        }
      ]
    },
